  ($q$gn06$q$, $q$greetings-names$q$, 5, $q$Good luck, see you again$q$, $j$[{"id":"rule-219","type":"rule","title":"Saying goodbye","body":"Thais don't make a big deal out of saying goodbye — sometimes they just leave. The formal way to say goodbye is the same as hello. Informally, just tell the other person you're leaving, adding ná (\"mind you\"/\"OK?\") to soften it.","source":"Essential Thai (Higbie), p.41"},{"id":"mc-227","type":"translationChoice","thai":"สวัสดีค่ะคุณชื่ออะไรแล้วก็สบายดีเหรอ","roman":"sà-wàt-dii khâ, khun chɯ̂ɯ à-rai láew-gɔ̂ɔ sà-baai dii rə̌ə","options":[{"text":"See you again.","correct":false},{"text":"Hello, what's your name, and are you well?","correct":true},{"text":"Have you eaten yet?","correct":false},{"text":"What's your name?","correct":false}],"source":"Essential Thai (Higbie), p.22","parts":["สวัสดี","ค่ะ","คุณ","ชื่อ","อะไร","แล้วก็","สบาย","ดี","เหรอ"]},{"id":"so-233","type":"sentenceOrder","prompt":"Hello, my name is Lek. I'm from England. (said by a man)","tileUnit":"word","words":{"a":{"roman":"sà-wàt-dii","thai":"สวัสดี"},"b":{"roman":"khráp","thai":"ครับ"},"c":{"roman":"phǒm","thai":"ผม"},"d":{"roman":"chɯ̂ɯ","thai":"ชื่อ"},"e":{"roman":"lék","thai":"เล็ก"},"f":{"roman":"khráp","thai":"ครับ"},"g":{"roman":"phǒm","thai":"ผม"},"h":{"roman":"maa","thai":"มา"},"i":{"roman":"jàak","thai":"จาก"},"j":{"roman":"ang-krìt","thai":"อังกฤษ"},"k":{"roman":"khráp","thai":"ครับ"},"x0":{"thai":"อะไร","roman":"à-rai"},"x1":{"thai":"ยัง","roman":"yang"}},"poolOrder":["x1","i","j","f","g","a","d","h","x0","c","b","e","k"],"correctOrder":["a","b","c","d","e","f","g","h","i","j","k"],"source":"Essential Thai (Higbie), p.38"},{"id":"sp-235","type":"speak","thai":"สวัสดีค่ะคุณสบายดีเหรอฉันสบายดีค่ะขอบคุณค่ะ","roman":"sà-wàt-dii khâ, khun sà-baai dii rə̌ə? chán sà-baai dii khâ, khɔ̀ɔp-khun khâ","meaning":"Hello, are you well? I'm well, thank you.","source":"Essential Thai (Higbie), p.39","parts":["สวัสดี","ค่ะ","คุณ","สบาย","ดี","เหรอ","ฉัน","สบา